“costing” means an assessment of the cost of apolicy proposal referred to in section 4 ora Bill tabled in Parliament, ifimplemented would change the budgetsurplus or deficit or would best suit theresources of the country in relation to theexisting laws but -

(a)it is not an assessment ofthe merits of a policy anddoes not provide policyrecommendations;

(c)it does not assess the non-financial impacts of a policy;

and shall include-

(i)an assessment of the overall costof the proposal;

(ii)the description of themethodology used to prepare thepolicy costing; and

(iii)the inputs used for the analysis;

